<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ALDUIN - THE TEST DRAGON.

    This is deliberately NOT the boss. CLAUDE.md invariant 2 says at most one BOSS Alduin per
    save, owned by GameComponent_DragonbornRegistry. This def is a third, dev-only creature
    that the registry never sees: it can never be the boss, never drops a soul, and never sets
    SlainForever. It exists so the twelve sprites and the three-state graphic switch can be
    judged in the running game before any gameplay is built on them.

    DOVAH ARE TIMELESS - the user's design, 2026-08-04. They do not age and they do not breed.
    That is expressed here, and it is not merely flavour:

      ONE life stage.  Verse.Pawn_AgeTracker.RecalculateLifeStageIndex only fires
      SetAllGraphicsDirty() when the life stage index actually CHANGES - and that call is the
      ONLY thing in the whole assembly that can undo our runtime sprite swap for an animal
      (verified by scanning all 12,819 types for callers). With a single stage the index is
      always 0, so it fires at most once, at spawn. The lore requirement and the graphics
      mechanism protect each other.

      NO hediffGiverSets.  AnimalThingBase inherits OrganicStandard, which is what applies
      age-related decline - cataracts, bad back, frailty. Cleared with Inherit="False".

      fixedGender Male on the PawnKindDef.  RimWorld.JobGiver_Mate opens with
      "if (pawn.gender != Gender.Male || pawn.Sterile()) return null", and its target test
      PawnUtility.FertileMateTarget requires a FEMALE of the same def. Every Alduin is male,
      so a mate target can never exist and the job can never be issued. Chosen over
      hasGenders=false, which also works but makes RimWorld call him "it" - dragons are "he"
      throughout Skyrim.

    THE BODY IS OURS - Dovahkiin_Dovah, in Defs/Bodies/Dovah_Dovahkiin.xml. It replaced vanilla
    "Bird" on 2026-08-04 because Bird was wrong three ways at once: its jaws part is literally a
    BEAK (so the combat log credited his bite to a beak - the user caught it in a pawn's
    wounds), it has no wings to bash with, and no wings to CRIPPLE, so SPEC.md 6.6's grounding
    rule could not exist.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Alduin_Test</defName>
    <label>Alduin</label>
    <description>The World-Eater. First-born of Akatosh, and the only dov who ever claimed to be a god. He does not age, he was not born, and he does not breed - he simply is, and has been since before the first men drew breath.\n\nThis one is a test specimen and is not the true Alduin.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>4.6</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>10000</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-100</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>100</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.70</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.50</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.90</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <FilthRate>10</FilthRate>
    </statBases>
    <uiIconScale>1.9</uiIconScale>
    <!--
      ⚠ EVERY linkedBodyPartsGroup MUST EXIST ON THE BODY NAMED IN <race><body>.

      The first version of this def used Teeth, FrontLeftLeg and FrontRightLeg - the groups a
      QUADRUPED has - against vanilla "Bird", which has only Beak, Feet and HeadAttackTool.
      RimWorld logged one config error per tool AT LOAD and the mod carried on, so the only
      symptom in play was a dragon who could barely fight: three of his four tools were inert
      and the sole survivor was the tail, at chanceFactor 0.4.

      That is the notebook's standing lesson, hit again: a clean build and a "does every def
      parse" check BOTH pass this. Parsing proves the XML is well-formed, not that the names in
      it RESOLVE. RimWorld's own config check at load is what catches it - READ THE LOG.

      Now checked against our own Dovahkiin_Dovah body instead.
    -->
    <!--
      HIS MELEE ROLLS. The user, 2026-08-04: his attacks should not all be bites.
      Weighted by chanceFactor, most likely first:

        MAW        pierce   most likely   - the signature attack
        WING BASH  blunt    middling      - no stun
        TAIL SWEEP blunt    RAREST        - stuns briefly

      The maw is linked to Dovahkiin_Maw on our own body, NOT to vanilla Bird's Beak group.
      That is what fixes the user's report that wounds were credited to a "beak": wound text
      comes from the BODY PART, so relabelling the tool would have changed nothing.

      Every linkedBodyPartsGroup here must exist on Dovahkiin_Dovah - RimWorld logs a config
      error at load and carries on, leaving the tool silently dead. That already happened once
      with Teeth/FrontLeftLeg/FrontRightLeg against Bird.
    -->
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>maw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <!--
          ⚠ THE armorPenetration LINE BELOW IS LOAD-BEARING. DO NOT DELETE IT TO "SIMPLIFY".

          Verse.Tool.armorPenetration defaults to -1, and VerbProperties.AdjustedArmorPenetration
          then derives AP as damage x 0.015 (decompiled, not assumed). So a tool left at the
          default has its POWER silently acting as its PENETRATION, and the two cannot be tuned
          apart. At power 45 that is AP 0.675 against Dragon Aspect's +0.60 Sharp, i.e. her
          signature defence cancelled outright: effective armour zero, every bite at full damage.
          That is what the user reported on 2026-08-05, as a naked but Aspected Dovahkiin being
          one shot roughly 70% of the time.

          Cutting power to 38.25 was tried first and REVERTED the same day, because it cuts the
          penetration with it (AP 0.574, still leaving 0.026) and so cannot fix the cause.

          Verse.ArmorUtility.ApplyArmor, read from the decompiler:
            effective = max(armourRating - armorPenetration, 0)
            roll < effective/2   -> damage 0, deflected
            roll < effective     -> damage halved AND Sharp converted to Blunt

          At AP 0.30 that gives, per bite:

            Dragon Aspect 3 words (+0.60)   effective 0.30   15% deflect + 15% halved
            Dragon Aspect 2 words (+0.40)   effective 0.10    5% deflect +  5% halved
            Dragon Aspect 1 word  (+0.10)   effective 0       unchanged
            naked, no Aspect      ( 0.00)   effective 0       unchanged, still bitten in half

          So the shout now matters and an unprotected pawn is no safer than before, which is the
          intended shape: armour is the answer to a dragon, not hit points.

          KNOWN AND ACCEPTED CONSEQUENCE: this helps EVERY armoured pawn, not just the Dovahkiin.
          A colonist in good plate (~0.75 Sharp) reaches effective 0.45, so a dragon is markedly
          less dangerous to a well equipped colony than it was. Flagged to the user 2026-08-05
          and kept deliberately.
        -->
        <power>38.475</power>
        <armorPenetration>0.27075</armorPenetration>
        <cooldownTime>2.4</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Dovahkiin_Maw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>1.4</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>wing bash</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>28.5</power>
        <!-- EXPLICIT, and it must stay so. Without it Verse.VerbProperties.AdjustedArmorPenetration
             derives AP as power x 0.015 = 0.4275, which pierced Dragon Aspect HARDER than the maw
             (0.285) - the signature bite being the least dangerous attack he owns. -->
        <armorPenetration>0.18</armorPenetration>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Dovahkiin_Wings</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.8</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>tail sweep</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>32.3</power>
        <!-- EXPLICIT. Derived would be 0.4845 - see the wing bash note above. -->
        <armorPenetration>0.22</armorPenetration>
        <cooldownTime>2.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Dovahkiin_Tail</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <!-- Rarest of the three, and the only one that stuns. Higher power than the wing bash
             to make it worth landing; the brief stun is applied in code, since a vanilla tool
             has no stun field. -->
        <chanceFactor>0.35</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <!-- NO CLAW ATTACK. Removed 2026-08-04 at the user's instruction: "dovahs have no claw
           attacks". His feet carry him; they are not a weapon. -->
    </tools>
    <race>
      <!-- OUR OWN BODY, 2026-08-04. Vanilla "Bird" was a stopgap and was wrong three ways: its
           jaws part is called a BEAK (so wounds read as beak damage - the user caught it), it
           has no wings to bash with, and it has no wings to CRIPPLE, so SPEC.md 6.6's grounding
           rule could not exist. See Defs/Bodies/Dovah_Dovahkiin.xml. -->
      <body>Dovahkiin_Dovah</body>
      <baseBodySize>4.6</baseBodySize>
      <baseHungerRate>0</baseHungerRate>
      <baseHealthScale>42.0</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <wildness>1.0</wildness>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1.0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <packAnimal>false</packAnimal>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>3.0</maxPreyBodySize>
      <canBePredatorPrey>false</canBePredatorPrey>
      <nameOnTameChance>0</nameOnTameChance>

      <!-- TIMELESS. See the header. -->
      <lifeExpectancy>1000000</lifeExpectancy>
      <hediffGiverSets Inherit="False" />
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>

      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <!--
      Keeps a FLYING dragon's sprite pointed where he is going. Flight is the only EIGHT-way
      state, so it is the only one that needs maintaining; grounded and soar are four-way and
      the engine's own Rot4 handles them.
      ONE <comps> block only - a second one parses as valid XML and RimWorld silently keeps one
      and drops the other.
    -->
    <comps>
      <li Class="Dovahkiin.CompProperties_AlduinFlight" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Alduin_Test</defName>
    <label>Alduin</label>
    <race>Dovahkiin_Alduin_Test</race>
    <combatPower>2000</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0</ecoSystemWeight>
    <!-- see the header: this is what makes breeding structurally impossible -->
    <fixedGender>Male</fixedGender>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!--
            GROUNDED is the DEFAULT and must stay so. Thing_AlduinGraphics swaps
            PawnGraphicSet.nakedGraphic to the soar and flight sets at runtime; whatever is
            named here is what he reverts to if anything ever re-resolves him.
            drawSize is an ABSOLUTE value and MUST MATCH dragonDrawSizeGrounded in
            Defs/MiscDefs/DovahkiinTuningDef.xml. Change BOTH or neither, or he resizes the
            first time he takes off.
            ⚠ DO NOT SCALE IT. The user asks for a size change in so many words. This line
               still read "4.6" long after the value had moved, and a "+10%" recorded
               elsewhere as an instruction got applied twice. Full account in the tuning def.
               5.566 IS SANCTIONED: the user chose to keep it on 2026-08-18. Do not revert it.
            Originally 4.6, measured against Dragon's Descent, whose adults draw at 4.2 and
            whose ancient draws at 4.6, against a colonist's 1.5.
          -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Alduin/AlduinGround</texPath>
          <drawSize>5.566</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.9, 0.8, 0.5)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.30)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>

